<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's Raiffeisen Unicbank H1 profits dip.</title>
<headline>Hungary's Raiffeisen Unicbank H1 profits dip.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending July 21.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-June 1997   Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>Profit before tax and</p>
<p>	provisions		    3,523	vs	3,668</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   4,045	vs	4,034</p>
<p>    Net fee income		  1,024	vs	1,102</p>
<p>    Net other income		  146 loss vs	  428 loss</p>
<p>    Operating costs		 1,400	vs	1,040</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total	 154,268	vs     94,374</p>
<p>    Corporate loans	     102,077	vs     70,247</p>
<p>     Of these:  forint loans   67,138	vs     49,698</p>
<p>	foreign currency loans   34,939	vs     20,549</p>
<p>    Corporate deposits	   82,599	vs     65,511</p>
<p>     Of these:forint deposits  46,507	vs     40,114</p>
<p>     foreign currency deposits 36,092	vs     25,397</p>
<p>    Provisions			  230	vs	  223</p>
<p>    Average number of employees   392	vs	  332</p>
<p>    Capital adequacy ratio (pct)   13.70(*)vs	   17.15</p>
<p>NOTE: (*) forecast. The figures are not audited.</p>
<p>Raiffeisen Unicbank Rt is a member of Austria's Raiffeisen Banking Group.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
